 For the resources and data sources examples, please check the [examples](https://github.com/zscaler/terraform-provider-zpa/tree/master/examples) directory.
 
+## Examples Usage - Remote Signing Service Authentication
+
+Private key authentication can also be used **without giving the provider the private key**. The
+OAuth2 client assertion is assembled by the provider and sent to a signing service - HashiCorp/HCP
+Vault Transit, a cloud KMS, or any HTTP signing endpoint - which returns the signature. The private
+key never leaves the key store, so it can be generated as non-exportable.
+
+```hcl
+# Configure the zpa Provider (OneAPI Authentication) - Remote Signing Service
+#
+# NOTE: `signing_url` conflicts with both `private_key` and `client_secret`.
+provider "zpa" {
+  client_id     = "[ZSCALER_CLIENT_ID]"
+  vanity_domain = "[ZSCALER_VANITY_DOMAIN]"
+  customer_id   = "[ZPA_CUSTOMER_ID]"
+  # HCP Vault Dedicated / Vault Enterprise Transit engine
+  signing_url             = "https://[CLUSTER].[REGION].hashicorp.cloud:8200/v1/transit/sign/zscaler-oneapi"
+  signing_vault_namespace = "admin"
+
+  # Workload identity: no static Vault token is stored anywhere
+  signing_auth_method    = "vault_jwt"
+  signing_vault_role     = "zscaler-terraform"
+  signing_jwt_token_file = "/var/run/secrets/tokens/vault-token"
+}
+```
+
+The Transit key must be an RSA key (`rsa-2048`, `rsa-3072` or `rsa-4096`) whose public key is
+registered on the Zscaler API client, and the Vault role must be allowed to call
+`transit/sign/<key>`. Zscaler only accepts `RS256`, so the provider always asks for
+`signature_algorithm=pkcs1v15` with `hash_algorithm=sha2-256`.
+
+### Signing service arguments
+
+| Argument                    | Description                                                                                                      | Environment Variable                                        |
+|-----------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
+| `signing_url`               | _(String)_ Signing endpoint that signs the client assertion. Conflicts with `private_key` and `client_secret`.     | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_URL`                                       |
+| `signing_mode`              | _(String)_ `vault_transit` or `http`. Inferred from `signing_url` when omitted.                                    | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_MODE`                                      |
+| `signing_key_id`            | _(String)_ Value of the `kid` header of the generated assertion.                                                   | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_KEY_ID`                                    |
+| `signing_auth_method`       | _(String)_ `none`, `token`, `vault_jwt` or `vault_approle`. Inferred from the other attributes when omitted.        | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_AUTH_METHOD`                               |
+| `signing_token`             | _(String, sensitive)_ Static credential for the signing service (`X-Vault-Token`, or a bearer token in `http` mode).| `ZSCALER_SIGNING_TOKEN`, `VAULT_TOKEN`                      |
+| `signing_auth_mount`        | _(String)_ Vault auth mount used to log in (`jwt` by default, `approle` for AppRole, `kubernetes` for Kubernetes).  | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_AUTH_MOUNT`                                |
+| `signing_vault_role`        | _(String)_ Vault role used with workload identity or AppRole login.                                                 | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_ROLE`, `VAULT_ROLE`                        |
+| `signing_jwt_token_file`    | _(String)_ Path to the workload identity token, re-read on every login.                                             | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_JWT_TOKEN_FILE`, `VAULT_JWT_TOKEN_FILE`    |
+| `signing_jwt`               | _(String, sensitive)_ Workload identity token given inline instead of by path.                                      | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_JWT`                                       |
+| `signing_role_id`           | _(String, sensitive)_ Vault AppRole role ID.                                                                        | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_ROLE_ID`, `VAULT_ROLE_ID`                  |
+| `signing_secret_id`         | _(String, sensitive)_ Vault AppRole secret ID.                                                                      | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_SECRET_ID`, `VAULT_SECRET_ID`              |
+| `signing_vault_namespace`   | _(String)_ Vault namespace (`admin` on HCP Vault Dedicated).                                                        | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_NAMESPACE`, `VAULT_NAMESPACE`              |
+| `signing_vault_address`     | _(String)_ Vault base address for login calls. Derived from `signing_url` when omitted.                             | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_VAULT_ADDRESS`, `VAULT_ADDR`               |
+| `signing_vault_key_version` | _(Integer)_ Pins the Transit key version. Defaults to the latest.                                                   | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_KEY_VERSION`                               |
+| `signing_request_format`    | _(String)_ `generic` (default) or `azure_keyvault`, in `http` mode.                                                 | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_REQUEST_FORMAT`                            |
+| `signing_response_format`   | _(String)_ `signature` (default) or `jwt` for a service that mints the whole assertion, in `http` mode.              | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_RESPONSE_FORMAT`                           |
+| `signing_signature_field`   | _(String)_ Dotted path to the signature in the response, e.g. `data.signature`. Detected automatically when omitted. | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_SIGNATURE_FIELD`                           |
+| `signing_headers`           | _(Map)_ Extra HTTP headers sent to the signing service.                                                             | -                                                           |
+| `signing_request_timeout`   | _(Integer)_ Timeout in seconds for a single signing call. Defaults to 30.                                           | `ZSCALER_SIGNING_REQUEST_TIMEOUT`                           |
+
+### Other signing services
+
+Any endpoint that signs a SHA-256 digest with RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 works. In `http` mode the provider
+POSTs `{"alg":"RS256","key_id":...,"signing_input":...,"digest":...,"digest_algorithm":"SHA-256"}`
+(both values base64url encoded) and reads the signature from `signature`, `data.signature`, `value`
+or `result`, accepting base64, base64url or hex. `signing_request_format = "azure_keyvault"` posts
+the `{"alg":"RS256","value":"<digest>"}` body that Azure Key Vault and Managed HSM expect.
+
 ## Authentication - OneAPI New Framework
 
 As of version v4.0.0, this provider supports authentication via the new Zscaler API framework [OneAPI](https://help.zscaler.com/oneapi/understanding-oneapi)
